{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074071-thought-exercise-inspirational-music-to-short-stories-plotlines","id":1074071,"title":"[Thought Exercise] Inspirational music to Short Stories/Plotlines","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-06T03:15:36-07:00","id":1074071,"title":"[Thought Exercise] Inspirational music to Short Stories/Plotlines","content":"Now, I have seen some post about inspirational music like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/914738-what-s-your-favorite-music-for-mage-the-awakening\">This Topic</a> and always wanted to use them to create a comprehensive narrative for my chronicle by finding different interpretations. Music can be interpreted in many ways without context (<a href=\"http://songmeanings.com/songs/view/3530822107859470105/\" target=\"_blank\">sites like this help</a>) and I was always curious about your perspective. Imagine it as a storytelling thought exercise; if the previous topics where about raw inspirational materials, this post is about refining them into short-stories/plotlines for a chronicle (as specific or abstract as you please). <br /> <br /> Here is my take:<br /> <br /> Delerium - Dust in Gravity<br /> \u201c...I close my eyes and let go and no one controls you\u2026\u201d<br /> <i><b>Man dreams that he is free</b></i><br /> <br /> Carnival of Rust - Poets of the Fall<br /> \u201c...It\u2019s all a game (about) avoiding failure, when true colors will bleed...\u201d<br /> <i><b>But Man is enslaved between success or failure of his aspirations</b></i><br /> <br /> Renegades - X Ambassadors<br /> \u201c...Run away with me, lost souls and reverie, running wild and running free\u2026\u201d<br /> <i><b>Man breaks this shackles only In his daydreams</b></i><br /> <br /> The Magus - Hainides <br /> \u201c...They heard words so pure and true, that tore their very souls in two...\u201d (translated)<br /> <i><b>Where Man discovers the dangerous Truth</b></i><br /> <br /> Make it Rain - Ed Sheeran<br /> \u201c...I know it can rain fire from the sky, \u2018till we find the purest of kings\u2026\u201d<br /> <i><b>Man wants to perfect himself despite the dangers</b></i><br /> <br /> Bad Habit - The Kooks<br /> \u201c...You know I wish I had it all...\u201d<br /> <i><b>And wants it all, forming a habit</b></i><br /> <br /> Demons - Imagine Dragons<br /> \u201c...I wanna hide the truth, I wanna shellter you...\u201d<br /> <i><b>So he fools himself by hiding the Truth</b></i><br /> <br /> Angel of Small Death &amp; the Codeine Scene - Hozier <br /> \u201c...lay my heart down, with the rest at her feet\u2026\u201d<br /> <i><b>But the Truth is an addictive drug</b></i><br /> <br /> Way Down We Go - Kaleo<br /> \u201c...Do we get what we deserve\u2026 or way down we go\u2026\u201d<br /> <i><b>Thus Man commits hybris</b></i><br /> <br /> Blood Red Roses - C21 FX <br /> \u201c...Vengeance is her only ward, beware the blood red rose\u2019s thorn...\u201d<br /> <i><b>Unable to come in terms with himself, Man unleashes vengeance on others</b></i><br /> <br /> Arsonist\u2019s Lullaby - Hozier<br /> \u201c...All you have is your fire, and a place it has to reach. Don\u2019t you ever tame your demons but always keep them on a leash...\u201d<br /> <i><b>Finally, in a moment of clarity, he accepts what he's done and moves forward or fails spectacularly</b></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Post